@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix cc:      <http://creativecommons.org/ns#> .
@prefix vann:    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .

@prefix arch:    <https://meta.linked.archi/core#> .
@prefix zachtax:    <https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/tax#> .
@prefix zach:    <https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/onto#> .
@prefix zachdt:  <https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/deliverable-templates#> .
@prefix :        <https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/metamodel#> .

<https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/metamodel#>
    rdf:type                      owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports                   <https://meta.linked.archi/core#> ;
    cc:license                    "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri    "https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/metamodel#" ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "zachmm" ;
    dcterms:title                 "Zachman Framework Metamodel Manifest"@en ;
    dcterms:description           '''Metamodel manifest for the Zachman Framework. Aggregates the taxonomy
(6 Aspects, 6 Perspectives, 36 Cells), SHACL validation shapes, and deliverable
templates into a single entry point. The Zachman Framework is a classification
schema — it does not define element types or viewpoints. It provides a 6x6 grid
for classifying descriptive representations produced by other modeling languages.'''@en ;
    dcterms:created               "2026-02-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified              "2026-02-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:creator               "Kalin Maldzhanski" ;
    dcterms:publisher             "Linked.Archi"@en, <https://linked.archi> ;
    owl:versionIRI                <https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/metamodel/0.3.0#> ;
    owl:versionInfo               "0.3.0"@en ;
.

#################################################################
# Framework
#################################################################

:ZachmanFramework
    a               arch:Framework ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Zachman Framework"@en ;
    skos:definition '''The Zachman Framework for Enterprise Architecture, created by John Zachman
in 1987. A two-dimensional classification schema formed by the intersection of
six primitive communication interrogatives and six reification transformations,
producing a bounded 6x6 matrix of 36 cells. Each cell represents a primitive
descriptive representation of the enterprise. It is not a methodology — it does
not prescribe a process for creating artifacts, but rather classifies the complete
logical space of descriptive representations of an enterprise.'''@en ;
    dcterms:publisher   "Zachman International"@en ;
    dcterms:creator     "John Zachman" ;
    dcterms:source      <https://zachman-feac.com/zachman/about-the-zachman-framework/> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso        <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zachman_Framework>,
                        <https://www.brcommunity.com/articles.php?id=b696> ;
.


#################################################################
# Metamodel
#################################################################

:ZachmanMetamodel
    a                             arch:Metamodel ;
    skos:prefLabel                "Zachman Framework Metamodel"@en ;
    arch:basedOnFramework         :ZachmanFramework ;
    arch:conceptClassification    <https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/tax#> ;

    ## Viewpoints — 36 viewpoints, one per cell
    ## File: zachman-viewpoints.ttl
    arch:architectureViewpoints   <https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/viewpoints#> ;

    ## SHACL validation shapes
    ## File: zachman-shapes.ttl
    arch:formalRules              <https://meta.linked.archi/zachman/shapes#> ;

    arch:hasDeliverableTemplate   zachdt:ArtifactCoverageReport ;
    skos:scopeNote                '''The Zachman Framework is a classification schema, not a modeling
language. It does not define element types (arch:modelConcepts is absent) or
viewpoints (arch:architectureViewpoints is absent). Instead, it provides a
6x6 classification grid formed by the intersection of six Aspects (columns —
also known as classification names or communication interrogatives) and six
Perspectives (rows — also known as audience perspectives or reification
transformations), producing 36 Cells. Any artifact from any modeling language
can be tagged against this grid.

Zachman Cells are classification slots for architecture artifacts, views, or
view components — not deliverables and not ISO 42010 architecture viewpoints.
A cell is fundamentally a coordinate — a (column, row) address in the grid.
Its identity is positional: "Inventory x Architect" or "Process x Executive."
A viewpoint's identity, by contrast, is a set of conventions: which concepts
to include, which notations to use, which correspondence rules apply. Those
are not the same thing — the cell is the slot, a viewpoint is the specification
that might fill or correspond to a slot. Zachman himself frames cells as the
"primitive" classification categories of the framework, not as view
specifications in the ISO 42010 sense.

Architecture deliverables (such as an Architecture Definition Document) are
compositions that aggregate multiple views and therefore typically cover many
Cells. A Cell may be used to derive or organize viewpoint families, but it is
not automatically a complete viewpoint unless additional viewpoint semantics
(concerns, stakeholders, model kinds, notations, correspondence rules) are
explicitly defined. This is why arch:architectureViewpoints is absent.

Classification properties (defined in zachman-onto.ttl):
  - zach:classifiedByCell — links a Viewpoint to a Zachman Cell

The classification chain:
  Aspect + Perspective → organize → Cell → classifies → Viewpoint → governs → View

Usage:

    ex:DataModelViewpoint a arch:Viewpoint ;
        arch:viewpointCoversAspect zachtax:Inventory ;
        arch:viewpointAddressesPerspective zachtax:Architect ;
        zach:classifiedByCell zachtax:R3C1_InventoryRepresentation .

    ex:MyLogicalDataModel a arch:Diagram ;
        arch:viewConformsToViewpoint ex:DataModelViewpoint .

    ex:ProcessFlowViewpoint a arch:Viewpoint ;
        arch:viewpointCoversAspect zachtax:Process ;
        arch:viewpointAddressesPerspective zachtax:BusinessManagement ;
        zach:classifiedByCell zachtax:R2C2_ProcessDefinition .

    ex:OrderProcessFlow a arch:Diagram ;
        arch:viewConformsToViewpoint ex:ProcessFlowViewpoint .

Deliverable (Model aggregating views):

    ex:ArchDefDoc a arch:Model ;
        arch:contains ex:MyLogicalDataModel, ex:OrderProcessFlow .
'''@en ;
.
